course: dictionary
lesson: 2615
title: Skin that reacts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dermatitis is a skin condition. Your skin becomes red, itchy, sore or swollen. The word tells you it is about skin, so you can often guess the topic before you read the rest.
explain: Read the words around it for clues. «Contact dermatitis is a skin reaction to something it touches.» Perfumed soap, plants and metals are things that can touch your skin, so they can be the cause.
explain: The next sentence gives a clue about what to do. «A mild soap-free wash is kinder to skin that reacts easily.» If skin reacts easily, it gets sore when something irritates it, so you want gentle products. Try your meaning in the sentence: red, itchy, sore skin fits the clues.
fact: Dermatitis means the skin becomes red, itchy, sore or swollen.
fact: Contact dermatitis can come from things like perfumed soaps, plants or metals.
fact: Eczema is a common type of dermatitis.
fact: Dermatitis is not catching: you cannot pass it to another person.
fact: Doctors treat dermatitis with creams and by helping you avoid the cause.
exercise: «Contact dermatitis is a skin reaction to something it touches.» What does dermatitis mean? | *Red, itchy, sore or swollen skin | A metal used in cooking pans | A sort of soap for washing hands | A type of plant that grows in woods
exercise: Which of these can cause contact dermatitis? | A library book | A bowl of cereal | *Perfumed soap
exercise: Ella asks, «Can I catch dermatitis from my friend?» What is the answer? | Yes, but only in winter | Only if you share a bath with them | *No, dermatitis is not catching | Yes, it spreads like a cold
test: Eczema is a common type of which skin problem? | *Dermatitis | Sunburn | Measles | A cold sore
test: «A mild soap-free wash is kinder to skin that reacts easily.» What kind of wash is kinder? | A strong perfumed soap | *A mild soap-free wash | A wash with metal scrubbers
exam: How do doctors usually treat dermatitis? | By giving you a new skin | By keeping you out of the sun forever | *With creams and by avoiding the cause | By cutting the skin open
